Model Processing Method
With reference to FIGS. 1A and 1B, a model processing method according to this embodiment of the present disclosure is described below. As shown in FIG. 1A, the model processing method includes steps S100-S130.
Step S100: Obtain a first source head model in response to a reception expression movement instruction. The first source head model includes neutral feature data, and a plurality of piece of expression feature data relative to the neutral feature date. The expression movement instruction indicates an expression type and/or an expression strength of the first source head model.
The first source head model is a three-dimensional head model having a certain appearance, which may be generated through a trained deep learning model. The neutral feature data represents a neutral state of the first source head model, indicating that no expression is applied to the first source head model. The plurality of pieces of expression feature data represent different expressions added to the neutral feature data. The expression movement instruction indicates a change in the first source head model, which may be a type of expression and/or an expression strength.
For example, as shown in FIG. 1B, the first source head model 100 includes a plurality of feature points, among which a first plurality of feature points 1001 are facial keypoints representing the eyes, nose, mouth, etc., and a second plurality of feature points 1002 are vertices representing the contours of the head, neck, shoulders, etc. When the expression movement instruction is received, the first source head model 1010 is transformed into a second source head model 1020 according to the expression movement instruction. Specifically, the first plurality of feature points 1011 are moved to form the second plurality of feature points 1021, and the second plurality of feature points 1102 are also moved to form the second plurality of feature point 1022. In this way, the first source head model 1020 is formed.
It should be noted that the first source head model 100 and the second source head model 1020 may both be two-dimensional or three-dimensional models. The first plurality of feature points 1020 and the second plurality of feature points 920 may be represented by coordinates. In this case, the coordinates of the first plurality of feature points 1101 and the second plurality of feature points 820 before the expression movement instruction is received may be stored in advance. After receiving the expression movement instruction, the coordinates of the first plurality of fea-ture points 1011 and the second plurality of feature points in the first source model 1010 may be updated to obtain the coordinates of the first plurality of feature poin ts 1021 and the second plurality of feature points of the second source head model 1021.
